+# Hi02 asteroid-profile runtime check (2026-10-20)
+
+The current Release apphost (`19edc4a-git`, 20261019) was built after patches
+2467 and 2468. It ran with a dedicated active NAP snapshot assembled from the
+base archives and the `asteroid-profile.nap` generated under
+`Data/NAP/.runtime-test-stage/asteroid-profile-20261019/`. The active snapshot
+contained 14 packages. All archive sizes, SHA-256 hashes, NAP headers, and
+manifest content versions were checked before launch; `asteroid-profile` was
+version 4 in both places. The app root had no loose `DATA`/`data` directory.
+The unrelated `planet-hdr-profile` package was excluded because it also
+overrides `EXE/newplayer.fl`. The exact manifest and startup log are included.
+The package input and temporary stage remain under `Data/NAP/.runtime-test-stage/asteroid-renderer-current-20261020/`.
+
+The run used SDL3 offscreen and Mesa OpenGL 4.3 (`NVE7`) at 640x480. It loaded
+game data, initialized the UI, entered Hi02, read back a space frame, and
+exported 300 profile rows with the render options enabled. The screenshot
+shows the live Hi02 scene but does not clearly resolve individual asteroids,
+so it is not visual proof of the culling result.
+
+## Profile
+
+| Metric | p50 | p95 | p99 |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| CPU update + draw (ms) | 132.107 | 140.873 | 156.307 |
+| Frame interval (ms) | 132.238 | 141.276 | 156.443 |
+
+Median FPS was 7.55. The cumulative dropped-simulation counter reached 2,861;
+this run is not a valid hardware performance baseline and cannot isolate the
+impact of patches 2467/2468. The Mesa renderer string `NVE7` was not mapped to
+a known GPU in this run. A controlled before/after run on the target GPU remains
+necessary.
+
+## Artifacts
+
+- [Hi02 frame](hi02-asteroid-field.png)
+- [300-frame profile CSV](frame-profile.csv)
+- [Active package manifest](active.json)
+- [Runtime log](runtime.log.txt)

